-- title:
--   Level automorphisms of Γ₀(M') normalise G and preserve K₀
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$, that is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $G \le \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ be generated by all $\tau$ for which, for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, the predicate `IsLevelAutAt` holds for $\gamma^{-1}$ and $\tau$: on every quotient $f/g$ of weight-$k$ forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions that lies in $K$, the series of $\tau$ of that element, read in $\mathbb{C}$ via $\xi \mapsto \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, is the ratio of the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ transformed by the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/(q\ell) \\ (q\ell)c & d\end{pmatrix}$. Put $K_0 = K^G$. Then for any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and any $\tau$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$, conjugation by $\tau$ and by $\tau^{-1}$ maps $G$ into $G$, and both $\tau$ and $\tau^{-1}$ map $K_0$ into $K_0$.
--
--   This is the normalisation step in the rigid-level frame: the automorphisms of the $q$-expansion field attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ normalise the subgroup generated by those attached to the normal subgroup $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, hence act on the descended field $K_0$, in the spirit of Shimura's description of fields of modular functions. It is used in the level-descent arguments that transport the Galois action to $K_0$ and to the descended supersingular charts and nodes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_mul_mul_inv_mem_and_map_fixedField_of_isLevelAutAt_gamma0.lean

